# Mutation plan for the user lifecycle plugin hook sites — `UserHasBeenCreated`,
# `UserWillLogIn`, `UserHasLoggedIn` and `UserHasBeenDeactivated` (docs/PLUGIN_PLAN.md, Phase 5).
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/plugin-hooks-lifecycle.plan
#
# The oracle is `parity::plugin_hooks::the_user_lifecycle_hooks_fire_as_go_fires_them`: one plugin
# binary under a real Go host and under the Rust host, the same client action against each.
#
# Not mutated: the rejection's id text and status, which `login`'s mask replaces with a 401
# `invalid_credentials_*` on the only login route the tour can drive (the desktop-token route
# needs an SSO account the stack cannot mint); and `update_active_for_bot`'s `!active` guard,
# which `user_has_been_deactivated`'s own `DeleteAt` check makes equivalent. The last two lines are
# the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.

